abstract: >-
  FrameAssembly is a domain-specific language (DSL), optimizing compiler, and PCAP-to-.fasm
  decompiler written in Rust that compiles declarative network packet specifications (.fasm)
  into deterministic, wire-valid PCAPNG (.pcap / .pcapng) packet captures—and decompiles
  .pcap / .pcapng captures back into canonical .fasm code (bidirectional .fasm <-> .pcap/.pcapng
  compilation and decompilation)—across 81 native Layer 2 through Layer 7 protocols (2,611
  verified .fasm corpus scenarios) with polymorphic IPv4/IPv6 dual-stack flows, stateful 4-tuple
  TCP sequence progression, and cryptographic SNMPv3 USM authentication and privacy.
